    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d822">

                <pb facs="0834" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5414a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-15T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                                1919—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>6081. I shall be glad to have you discuss informally with the Foreign Office the
                    situation which has arisen in the Baltic with a view <pb facs="0835" n="723"
                        xml:id="pg723"/> to ascertaining the British estimate thereof, British
                    policy and what it expects to accomplish.</p>
                <p>I am asking the Peace Commission to repeat to you a telegram of even date to Mr.
                    Polk which will acquaint you with the views of this Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
